			"259": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 3: SIMPLE BEHAVIOR\n\nIn this patch we're demonstrating how simple \"behavior\" can be achieved with nodes like Nearest and Furthest.\nWe generate a collection of smooth random values for X-axis movement using the Perlin Generator.\nThis goes into a Float 2 with a Y set to 0, this moves the shapes around.\n\nNext we check which X-value is Nearest to 0 (the center of the X-axis).\nWe use the Write node to write a new value into the Float2 collection that controls our movement.\nThe output of the Nearest node is used to get the correct index.\nWe copy the X-axis value from the Perlin Generator using Read, but we replace the Y with a 1.\n\nBy smoothing the result it looks like the most center value \"jumps\" up."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 805.38250732421875,
					"width": 2272.93798828125,
					"x": -727.813232421875,
					"y": 1022.16864013671875
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffe53357",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Group",
				"thumbnail_visible": true
			},
